# Aaura Privacy Policy

**Last Updated: October 17, 2026**

## Introduction

Aaura ("the App") is a macOS menu bar app by ARG Studios that draws a circle
around your cursor and shows reminders you set. This Privacy Policy explains
the App's data practices.

## Data Collection and Privacy

**The App does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data.**

- We do not collect any information about you, your Mac, or your use of the App
- We do not use analytics, tracking, or telemetry services
- We do not operate any servers, and the App makes no network requests of its own
- We do not use cookies or similar tracking technologies
- We do not share any information with third parties

## Pointer Movement

To keep the circle under your cursor and to recognise a shake, the App reads
the pointer's position while it is running. Positions are used in the moment
and are never recorded, saved, or sent anywhere. The App does not read your
keyboard, your screen contents, or what you click on.

## Calendars and Reminders

If you turn on calendar alarms, the App asks macOS for permission to read
your calendars and, if you include them, your reminders. It reads them on
your Mac through Apple's EventKit, which covers every account already added
to the Calendar app (such as iCloud or Google). The App reads only the
title, time and alerts of upcoming items, to show them as rings. It never
signs in to your accounts, never sees your passwords, never changes your
calendars, and never sends calendar data anywhere. You can turn access off
at any time in System Settings › Privacy & Security.

## Local Data Storage

Your settings and the reminders you create (their times and messages) are
stored on your Mac in the App's own container. This data is not transmitted
to us or to any external service. Deleting the App removes it.

## Sounds and Power

Alarm sounds are the system sounds that come with macOS. While an alarm with
sound is waiting, the App may ask macOS to keep your Mac from going to sleep
on its own, and it wakes the display when the alarm goes off. No data is
involved in either.

## Third-Party Services

The App does not integrate with any analytics platforms, advertising networks,
or third-party SDKs.

## Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted at
the same address as this policy. Your continued use of the App after changes
constitutes your acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy.

